WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.569
A whole is divided into 2 equal halves. We already have 1 of the parts. How many more

00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:10.341
equal parts make one whole? (Puzzle 1) Let us think carefully. A whole has 2 equal

00:00:10.341 --> 00:00:16.008
pieces. We have 1, so we need 2 minus 1 equals 1 more. The answer is 1. Great work!

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:22.026
A whole is divided into 4 equal quarters. We already have 1 of the parts. How many

00:00:22.026 --> 00:00:26.882
more equal parts make one whole? (Puzzle 2) Let us think carefully. A whole has 4

00:00:26.882 --> 00:00:32.649
equal pieces. We have 1, so we need 4 minus 1 equals 3 more. The answer is 3. Great

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:32.952
work!

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:38.861
A whole is divided into 4 equal quarters. We already have 2 of the parts. How many

00:00:38.861 --> 00:00:43.639
more equal parts make one whole? (Puzzle 3) Let us think carefully. A whole has 4

00:00:43.639 --> 00:00:49.314
equal pieces. We have 2, so we need 4 minus 2 equals 2 more. The answer is 2. Great

00:00:49.314 --> 00:00:49.613
work!

